What are your thoughts on the 1M output token window? Is this the tipping point where autonomous coding agents fully replace traditional junior development pipelines, or are closed-model API bills going to make local open models like DeepSeek-R1 the true winner?', 'AI & LLM BREAKTHROUGH', 2274, 0, 14, 605, NULL, '{"title": "Google DeepMind Gemini 4 Argon Keynote & Live 1M Token Demonstration", "embed_url": "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/aircAruvnKk", "provider": "youtube", "duration": "24:18"}', '[{"url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558494949-ef010cbdcc31?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80", "caption": "Gemini 4 Argon Benchmark Performance: Leading DeepSWE v1.1 (77.9%) and AutomationBench (51.3%)", "alt": "AI benchmark data visualization"}, {"url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80", "caption": "DeepMind multi-head sparse attention architecture enabling 1,000,000 output tokens in a single stream", "alt": "Neural network architecture diagram"}, {"url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1550745165-9bc0b252726f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80", "caption": "Gray Swan Indirect Prompt Injection Benchmark: Gemini 4 Argon sets all-time record of 0.7% attack success", "alt": "Cybersecurity defense chart"}]', NULL, NULL, 'published', 1790807008882, 0);
